]•Several minor improvements and minor fixes have been incorporated[.
]•For bayes and rules files Spam[Ass]assin now uses the paths configured in the file "path.[config]" to access Bayes filter and rules files.[
]•Spam[Ass]assin for Windows 3[.]4.0[.]30 (includes Apache SpamAssassin[ 3.]4.0) has been integrated[.
]•The CPU load of the SpamAssassin daemon was reduced significantly. This was achieved by using a set of native compiled anti spam rules ("Rule2XSB[ody" plugin]).[
]•A problem that caused the service to stop itself sometimes, has been solved.[
]•Under certain conditions a wrong scan date was shown in the spam report. This problem has been solved[.
